# Line endings are a fact of the file, not of the machine that checked it out.
#
# Without this file every clone uses its own core.autocrlf: on Windows a file
# can come back as CRLF, show as "modified" with an equal number of insertions
# and deletions, and put line-ending noise into history. `eol=lf` pins the
# working tree too, so a Windows checkout writes LF and the diff stays about
# the code.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
